Round 3 of seven-card stud is up. You start this hand with 1,040 chips. After the 10-chip ante you have 1,030, and the pot is 20. I've taken the Deal again button off round 2's table.

This is third street. Your two face-down cards are 7♣ and 7♥, and your face-up card is 10♦, so you have a **pair of sevens**. Your opponent is showing a Q♣. You're first to act: check, bet 20 or fold.
